    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Auth split",
      "items": [
        "Supabase Auth owns passwords and SMS MFA; the frontend requires aal2 before provisioning (auth-panel.tsx:328-330)",
        "The backend verifies bearer JWTs against the issuer JWKS with issuer and audience checks (backend/src/amira_api/auth.py:119-127)",
        "The backend never issues login tokens"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Data layer",
      "items": [
        "SQLAlchemy connects with TLS, a 10s connect timeout, and a 5s statement timeout (backend/src/amira_api/db.py:23-32)",
        "Catalog tables enable RLS and revoke anon/authenticated privileges (20261010_0001_location_catalog.py:438-459)",
        "A privileged connection bypasses RLS, so endpoints enforce authorization themselves"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Deployment",
      "items": [
